chx:F1 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Background"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Chapter 2 follows one real transaction - Alice paying Bob's Store - through wallet, network and blockchain: transactions as double-entry lines of inputs and outputs with an implied fee, transaction chains, change and coin selection, common transaction forms, constructing and propagating a transaction, mining that bundles transactions into blocks, and confirmations that make a payment harder to reverse as blocks pile up." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01 .
chx:F2 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Contemporary developments"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The Bitcoin Core software that full nodes run to verify every rule has continued to release after the book; its releases page lists 31.1 as the newest." ; sen0414:cites chx:P03 .
chx:F3 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter's claim that a payment becomes harder to reverse with each confirmation is quantified in Nakamoto's paper: for an attacker with a tenth of the hash power the probability of catching up falls from 0.2045873 at one confirmation to 0.0002428 at six, and a Python transcription of the paper's own procedure reproduces that table exactly." ; sen0414:cites chx:P02, chx:P01 .
chx:F4 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Conclusion"@en ; sen0414:findingText "For the course theme, a transaction chain - each input spending an earlier output - is a provenance graph, and W3C's PROV Ontology offers the vocabulary to describe it: entities derived from entities by activities, attributed to agents." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P04 .
chx:Scorecard a sen0414:QualityScorecard ; rdfs:label "Quality scorecard"@en ; sen0414:topicCoverage "25 primary-source concepts inventoried from the textbook ontology." ; sen0414:citationStrength "4 sources, all opened and verified at 2026-09-25T00:26:42; 4 cited by findings." ; sen0414:methodologyCompliance "RDODI procedure v1.6.0 Stage 1." ; sen0414:reproducibility "Every source is a stable public URL; every claim names its sources." .
